<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Banco Popular '96 net profit up 42 pct.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Banco Popular '96 net profit up 42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The net profit of Banco Popular, Colombia's sixth largest bank in terms of assets, rose 42.55 percent in 1996 over the previous year, the country's Banking Superintendency said.</p>
<p>It said the bank, which was privatized in November 1996, showed a net profit at year-end of 29 billion pesos and assets totaling 1.62 trillion pesos, up 15.62 percent over 1995.</p>
<p>The bank is owned by an industrial group headed by Luis Carlos Sarmineto Angulo.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
